  "result_notes": {
    "thm:main": "For INTEGERS 1<=a<b, not necessarily reduced, N(a,b) is minimum length of exact DISTINCT positive unit fractions with denominators>=2; N(b)=MAX over numerators. Eventual absolute c1 loglogb<=N(b)<=c2 loglogb, all a get upper only; N(1,b)=1. No final denominator cap, bitlength/runtime bound or effective threshold supplied.",
